iven-names></name><name><surname>Saleem</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hughson</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Philips</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How important is inadvertent ingestion of hazardous substances at work?</article-title><source>Ann Occup Hyg</source><year>2006</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>693</fpage><lpage>704</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16840437</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/annhyg/mel035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haw</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruer</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Amos</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Currie</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Fischbacher</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Fong</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Hastings</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Malam</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Pell</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Semple</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Legislation on smoking in enclosed public places in Scotland: how will we evaluate the impact?</article-title><source>J Public Health</source><year>2006</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>24</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/pubmed/fdi080</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>British Sociological Society: Statement of ethical practice</article-title><year>2002</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.sociology.org.ukmpo22f.htm"/></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Semple</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Creely</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Naji</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ayres</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Secondhand smoke levels in Scottish pubs: the effect of smoke-free legislation</article-title><source>Tob Control</source><year>2007</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://tc.bmj.com/homepage/Scottishsmoke.pdf"/><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17400951</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Conner</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Waranch</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Stillman</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Pennington</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lees</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Oski</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The impact of a total ban on smoking in the Johns Hopkins Children's Center</article-title><source>J Amer Med Assoc</source><year>1989</year><volume>262</volume><fpage>799</fpage><lpage>802</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.262.6.799</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dawley</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Burton</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Smoking control in a hospital setting</article-title><source>Addict Behav</source><year>1985</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>355</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3937446</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.10